    [BugFix] Preserve GLM-5.3-Flash MRV2 MTP capture lifecycle (#16936)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    When `index_share_for_mtp_iteration` is enabled, MTP runtime computes
    top-k in the first draft step and reuses those indices in later steps.
    The Ascend MRV2 capture override omitted the existing lifecycle hooks
    and captured decode with `skip_topk=False`, while runtime uses `True`.
    
    Call the existing prefill/decode hooks around graph capture and clear
    the request mapping before capture. This records the runtime branch and
    restores ordinary mode afterwards. Extend the existing capture tests to
    verify the single-step and multi-step lifecycle.
    
    Refs #15665. Related MRV2 work: #16755.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Corrects shared-index MTP graph capture for GLM-5.3-Flash on MRV2. No
    new option is introduced.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Isolated CPU execution of existing metadata regression cases and
    actual capture/MTP hook methods: **16 passed**. Framework and kernel
    boundaries are isolated; these are not full-module or NPU tests.
    - A counterfactual using the base capture method records draft decode
    with `skip_topk=False`; the updated method records `True`, matching
    runtime.
    - Current-head [pre-commit, including Linux hooks and
    mypy](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39021249056/job/117363337242):
    **passed**. CPU/device CI is pending in [the same
    run](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/actions/runs/39021249056).
    Current-head Nightly has not run; direct workflow dispatch was rejected
    with HTTP 403.
    - Current-head NPU graph/MTP accuracy and complete GSM8K remain
    unverified. Existing `glm-5.2-w4a8-mtp-v2` nightly enables eager draft
    execution, so it can check compatibility but cannot establish draft
    graph replay correctness.
    
